Well, this was an interesting game. 
I encountered many "ordinary" scary moments in the game,
had fun raising a dragon, almost lost my nerve, lost my
nerve, blew wishless conduct in Gehennom and finally brought
the game into an end - ascension. Rex the Healer is here!

I played about 10 healers, of which none survived.
Some made it to Minetown, some didn't. Things seemed
pretty hopeless. 

Rex the Healer remembered seeing strange dreams in which
he, or rather previous incarnations of himself were running
in strange caverns, filled with strange light... and beings.
There was no escape from the horde of creatures. Darkness...

Rex entered the dungeons. Bullet the little dog proved to be
a great fighting companion to Rex. Rex could fight only
so well, and was having trouble finding food. As Rex got more
magical points, he created food from all things stony.

Mines (dlvl 4 entrance) were... dangerous. A tombstone there proved
that, on the very first mine level. Rex in vain tried to kill
the ghost, and in an ensuing fight with other monsters, was separated
from Bullet and ended in the Minetown, himself.

Rex did some shopping, went to a co-aligned temple and noticed
a cat wandering in the streets. Rex tamed it with a tripe ration.
As Rex was identifying fresh wands, one of them produced a strange
message on the floor. Rex zapped repeatedly his cat, Garfield, which 
eventually turned into a Yellow Dragon. From that point on, Rex
would let Garfield find food for itself and occasionally heal
Garfield. The town watch was helpless, and so were the shopkeepers.
A great Boot of Luck in the behind!!! "$$$" said the Priest.

Rex sacced some corpses and got Vorpal Blade. Well, some of the
beheadings came in the nick of time, especially when Garfield
was only eating. The monster grew. It had about 150+ HP when
Rex emerged from the mines to seek out Sokoban.
On the way up from Mines Rex cleared the bones area and
grabbed all things useful. Only later he identified one of the
amulets as reflection. And, I had a good guess that the new-found
riding gloves were GoD...

Rex wore useful armor, not hampering spellcasting: Elven boots,
orcish (later elven) cloak, GoD (as it turned out), elven leather helm,
a studded leather armor and a +2 small shield. 

Garfield ate a shopkeeper on level 5. Unfortunately, it ate
a chameleon in Sokoban (10) and turned into a foo. Rex turned
it into a mountain centaur, and /oPoly was empty.
Luckily Rex got a BoH from Sokoban.

The next travel plan: 

11-elliptical big room
14-ludios, Athena's temple //Polypile, get Water... (quick BUC check possible here)
15-quest
16-altar //Pray for holy water, sac corpses, get AC points
17-rogue
18-altar 
24-medusa

I had not received any wishes, so I decided to try going without them.
As luck would have it, luck would not have it.

I killed everything on Ludios except Croesus. I decided
to come back later to do my usual polypilings and stashings.
I decided to do the Quest - I had magic whistle and a =oLevitation.
Quest went fine - I even got gray dragon scales! Unfortunately
I had wasted all my b?oEA on my normal armor.

The Cyclops was a funny guy. He almost killed me. He
drained my levels. I had foolishly placed a boulder on
the staircase up. Yeah, like it stopped giants!
On the next level, I managed to write Elbereth and then
kill the creature. Garfield the electric vortex (or whatever)
and Fink (new pet, magic trap) the horned devil I left in the
Cyclop's island. Boy, was the staff useful! 

After leaving Ludios (again), I went down to Medusa (24)
and the Castle (28). I had an AC of -10, and apparently
low MC. As I went to Gehennom, a werewolf attacked me.
Grrr! After one turn it bit me, I turned into a wolf!
Rip! said my cloak and gray dragon scales. I summoned
wolves to help me. Luckily, the werewolf backed away,
and no monsters were nearby. I picked up my pick-axe and threw
it up in the air until it knocked me back to human
form. I made the hard decision to teleport up to dlvl14
(Ludios) and blow the wishless conduct. 

Mistake #1: Too much attempting polymorphing monster
at Sokoban - lost the benefit of /oPolys. Could
have helped - magic markers.
Mistake #2: Wasted b?oEAs, could have gotten GDSMail.
Mistake #3: Low magic cancellation, apparently.
I didn't keep my Elven cloak, I had displacement.

Well, at least I survived. Now, let's make something of
this game. 

I reverse genoed Silver dragons to get scales, and then
lots of tengu to get teleport control. I had teleportitis
already...

I polyed and upgraded my kit - speed boots, CoMR, markers and a
HoB. I used up all /oCreate Sacrifice at level 16, and
dropping my luckstone, managed to get 2 extra points of
protection. I produced huge amonuts of holy water and
Full Healing and improved my max HP.

And the rest... well, Yeenoghu appeared on level 34, which
was Asmodeus' temple.
The Wizard's gang and Moloch's gang died with the help
of Conflict. The Force was a bit annoying.

Planes were easy. On Air lightning struck me a couple of times.
On Astral Plane Death drained some of my HP. The Middle temple
was Athena's, so I went in the Right one. Pestilence proved
to be an annoyance, curiously after he was killed a couple
of times. Well, I had the Staff, Cure Sickness at 0% failure
and some potions, so I survived. I grabbed some loot from the
Plane, and tamed a titanothere before I ascended.

Hmm. Quite an interesting game, again started with a good stroke
of luck. Much of "nice" scary moments, requiring escape from
combat and constant healing. Quite a long game for me so far.

Ascended all charecters now. I should have fun trying to
figure out all those glorious conducts, now :)
Or just, like, do something silly, fool around... maybe
ascend.


